a pointer-receiver method value on an SRET (by-address: large/managed) value receiver from a call/temp crashes: the sret result is a pointer, so storing it into the by-value closure field needs a struct COPY (not a scalar store). 947 materialize fix is gated to register-returned structs (types.NeedsSret). Fix: sret-aware struct-copy into the closure field. claude-todo.md.
